# Relativity 50.0 — Pure Relation / Relata Relativity  
## Objects as Fixed Points of Relational Structure

**White paper / academic preprint**

---

## Abstract

Pure Relation / Relata Relativity is the ontological completion of the relativistic sequence. It asserts that objects are not prior to relations. Objects are stable fixed points of relational structure. Instead of beginning with things that relate, one begins with relations and derives relata as invariant nodes, attractors, or identity structures within a relational order. Categorically, an object \(X\) is determined by its relations to all other objects:

\[
X
\cong
\mathrm{Hom}(-,X).
\]

This is the Yoneda perspective: what a thing is is given entirely by how it stands to everything else. The central principle is:

\[
\boxed{
\text{Relata are not fundamental. They are fixed points of relational structure.}
}
\]

Particles, observers, fields, and even spacetime points become secondary stabilizations of a deeper relational order. Pure Relation / Relata Relativity unifies structural realism, relational quantum mechanics, gauge theory, categorical physics, spin networks, causal-set theory, holographic entanglement, and network relativity into a single ontological framework. It does not eliminate objects. It demotes them from primitive substances to emergent invariant patterns of relation.

---

## 1. Introduction

The metaphysical default of everyday thought is substance ontology.

We imagine that the world consists first of things, and only secondarily of relations among things.

There are particles. Then they interact.

There are observers. Then they observe.

There are spacetime points. Then fields are located at them.

There are objects. Then they relate.

Pure Relation / Relata Relativity reverses this order.

It says:

\[
\boxed{
\text{Relations are primitive. Relata are derived.}
}
\]

This does not mean that tables, electrons, stars, and observers do not exist.

It means that they do not exist as primitive, self-subsisting substances.

They exist as stable relational patterns.

They are fixed points of relational structure.

They are invariant nodes in a web of transformations.

They are what remains stable under the full structure of relations.

This is the final ontological consequence of the relativistic program.

Special relativity made motion relational.

General relativity made geometry relational.

Quantum reference frames made observers relational.

Holography made locality relational.

Semantic relativity made descriptions relational.

Recursive consistency made the absolute relational.

Pure Relation / Relata Relativity completes the sequence by making objects themselves relational.

---

## 2. Substance Ontology and Its Dissolution

Substance ontology holds that reality consists of basic entities bearing properties.

An electron is a little thing with charge, mass, and spin.

A spacetime point is a bare location.

An observer is a subject standing behind experience.

Modern physics has progressively undermined this picture.

In gauge theory, the vector potential \(A_\mu\) is not uniquely physical. The physical object is the gauge orbit,

\[
[A_\mu].
\]

In quantum field theory, particles are not tiny persistent substances. They are excitations of fields, and fields themselves are algebraic structures.

In algebraic quantum field theory, local observables are primary. The algebraic relations among observables determine physical structure.

In general relativity, spacetime points have no identity independent of fields. Diffeomorphic models represent the same physical situation.

In quantum information, subsystems are not absolute. They are defined by factorization, correlations, and accessibility.

In categorical physics, objects are determined by morphisms.

Thus the old substance-ontology is replaced by relational structure.

---

## 3. The Core Principle

The central principle of Pure Relation / Relata Relativity is:

\[
\boxed{
\text{Relata are not fundamental. They are fixed points of relational structure.}
}
\]

A relatum is not a primitive thing.

It is a stable position in a relational order.

It is an invariant under transformations.

It is a node that persists because the relations around it stabilize it.

Thus:

\[
\text{object}
=
\text{stable relational pattern}.
\]

This is not nihilism.

It is a redefinition of objectivity.

An object is real insofar as it is a robust invariant of relational structure.

