They are relational junctions where quantum geometric relations meet.

An intertwiner is a gauge-invariant relation among incident edge representations.

Thus nodes are derived from relational consistency.

They are fixed points of gauge-invariant coupling relations.

Thus:

\[
\boxed{
\text{Quantum-geometric nodes are relational fixed points, not primitive atoms of space.}
}
