## 19. Axioms of Pure Relation / Relata Relativity

The framework may be organized around twelve axioms.

### Axiom 1: Relations Are Primitive

Relations are not properties of prior objects.

### Axiom 2: Relata Are Derived

Objects are stable invariant nodes of relational structure.

### Axiom 3: Identity Is Relational

An object is determined by its relations to all other structures.

### Axiom 4: Yoneda Principle

An object is determined by its representable relational profile:

\[
X
\cong
\mathrm{Hom}(-,X).
\]

### Axiom 5: Objects Are Fixed Points

Relata are fixed points of relational refinement:

\[
\Phi(X)\cong X.
\]

### Axiom 6: Persistence Is Stability

Objects persist by stability of relational profile.

### Axiom 7: Spacetime Points Are Relational

Points are fixed points of field-causal-metric relations.

### Axiom 8: Particles Are Symmetry Fixed Points

Particles are invariant patterns under symmetry relations.

### Axiom 9: Observers Are Self-Stabilizing Relations

Observers are relational control structures, not primitive subjects.

### Axiom 10: Dynamics Is Relational Transformation

Change is transformation of relational structure.

### Axiom 11: Objectivity Is Invariance

Objectivity is invariance under admissible relational transformations.

### Axiom 12: Reflexivity Is Required

Relations may relate relations without requiring external relata.

