## Appendix B: Objects as Identity Relations

Suppose primitive relations compose associatively.

An object may be identified with an identity relation \(e\).

It satisfies:

\[
e\circ e=e.
\]

For any relation \(r:s\to t\),

\[
r\circ e_s=r,
\]

\[
e_t\circ r=r.
\]

Thus objects are idempotent units of relational composition.

They are derived from the relational structure.

